  "articleBody": "It's super disheartening to walk into a newly tiled room and notice that some tiles just aren't sitting right. An uneven tile floor, often called lippage, is a common issue that usually stems from a few key areas during installation. The most frequent culprits are poor substrate preparation – if the subfloor isn't perfectly flat, the tiles won't be either. You've got to make sure high spots are removed and any cracks or deflection are addressed before you even think about laying tile. Another big factor is incorrect mortar coverage; if the mortar isn't spread evenly with the right trowel, some tiles will naturally sit higher or lower. Uneven spacing can also contribute to the problem, making individual tiles stand out. Lastly, if the floor is walked on or loaded too soon before the mortar has properly cured, tiles can shift, leading to an uneven surface. For larger tile formats, uneven subfloors, or in wet areas where waterproofing is critical, professional help is invaluable. HH Remodeling LLC focuses on meticulous preparation and precise installation, ensuring a perfectly flat and uniform tile surface that lasts. Don't settle for an uneven floor; contact Abraham at 303-505-0866.",
